:::'''(Trailblazer):''' (This doesn't seem right, I'd better talk to Qingzu at the Seat of Divine Foresight.)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Put it aside.
:::'''(Trailblazer):''' (It's not that I don't trust Dan Shu... but this doesn't seem like something I should take lightly.)
:::'''(Trailblazer):''' (Something feels off &mdash; I'd better talk to Qingzu at the Seat of Divine Foresight.)
:'''Dan Shu:''' Your footsteps still linger. Could it be that you still have unanswered questions?
::'''Dan Shu:''' Ask, and I shall answer to the best of my ability.
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Is there really no way to cure Incomplete Ones?
:::'''Dan Shu:''' Not all incompletions are without remedy. Take my ingenium arm, for example &mdash; it doesn't require any invasive surgery and operates by detecting bioelectric signals on my skin.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' My eyes are another story &mdash; the optic nerves never fully developed. Transplants are a temporary solution, but they are soon rejected by the superior healing powers of the Xianzhou natives... The entire process is worse than death.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' There are many similar cases... Skeletal deformities, soft tissue defects, congenital heart disease &mdash; the list goes on...
:::'''Dan Shu:''' For short-life species, all these problems can be solved with artificial organs and implants. For long-life species, however, they remain as incompletions.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' To give a common example... Did you know that to varying degrees, most Xianzhou natives are plagued by oral diseases and jaw-related conditions?
:::'''Dan Shu:''' For most living creatures, wisdom teeth need to be removed as early possible... but for we long-life species, they are as stubborn as boulders. We must endure them for as long as we live.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' You see? This is the truth about the Vessel of Celestials... nothing more than a vessel of the Incomplete.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Why wouldn't abominations be Incomplete?
:::'''Dan Shu:''' For beings transformed by the Abundance, there's a difference. Do you know how Abominations of Abundance and Xianzhou people differ?
:::'''Dan Shu:''' I've given this question much thought, using all the knowledge I've learned from the Alchemy Commission to answer it. But, deep down, I know there is only one correct answer: There is no difference.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' The only difference between us is whether we embrace or reject the long life placed upon us by the Abundance.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' Borisin, known for their ferocity among the Denizens of Abundance, are similar to the foxians of the Yaoqing genetically... But the foxians are not abominations &mdash; they're Xianzhou people.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' From there, we can say that the difference between an abomination and a Xianzhou person is not one of taxonomy, but one of culture.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' If an abomination aligns with the Xianzhou, then they are a Xianzhou person. If a Xianzhou person aligns with the abominations, they become an abomination themselves. It is that simple.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' Abominations embrace their nature &mdash; they change and modify their flesh without care, for the sake of attaining power and strength. However, to the Xianzhou people, these methods are completely taboo.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' Now you know why there are no Incomplete Ones among the abominations...
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Разговор}} Do you know much about the Disciples of Sanctus Medicus?
:::'''Dan Shu:''' I'm just an alchemist &mdash; I don't understand them in any detail. I only know that they are a group of Xianzhou people who view themselves as Denizens of Abundance.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' My guess is that they attribute their suffering to their decision to renounce the Path of the Plagues Author. Thus, they seek to save themselves by becoming Denizens of Abundance again.
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I don't have any other questions.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' I have a gift for you, but I'll need a little time to prepare it... I'll contact you once it's ready to collect.
:::'''Dan Shu:''' See you soon, (Trailblazer).
